{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe MCP client URL every doc and committed example specifies —\n`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/` (WITH the trailing slash) — answers `307` with\n`location: http://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp`: an HTTPS->HTTP downgrade, with no HSTS\nheader to upgrade it back. The no-slash `/mcp` returns a correct `401`. Re-reproduced 2026-08-27\nfrom unauthenticated probes.\n\nA 307 preserves method and body, and clients differ on whether they retain `Authorization`\nacross a same-host scheme change, so a client that retains it puts its bearer PAT on the wire in\nplaintext. The docs point AT the affected form: `examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml:18`,\n`docs/mcp-client-setup.md:54`.\n\n## Confirmed root cause\n\nProven at runtime; the evidence, discriminating experiment and defect attribution are in the RCA\ncomment on this ticket. Three changeable artifacts:\n\n**A** `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template:127` is a PREFIX `location /mcp` with a\nURI-preserving `proxy_pass http://rebar_mcp;`, so external `/mcp/` reaches the app verbatim\nwhile the app mounts at `http_path = \"/mcp\"` (`src/rebar/mcp_server.py:524,618-627`); Starlette's\ndefault `redirect_slashes` emits the 307. `docs/mcp-auth.md:252-271` already prescribes\nEXACT-MATCH locations for this asymmetry and the template diverged from it.\n\n**B** uvicorn is built at `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:311-317` with no `forwarded_allow_ips`, so\nit defaults to `\"127.0.0.1\"` (`uvicorn/config.py:356-357`). The app runs in a container\n(`docker-compose.yml:337`), so nginx's connection arrives from the docker bridge gateway; that\npeer is untrusted, nginx's `X-Forwarded-Proto https` (`rebar.conf.template:132`) is dropped, and\napp-generated absolute URLs are built as `http://`. No `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` is set in `infra/`.\n\n**C** The 443 server block has no `add_header Strict-Transport-Security`.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Serve `/mcp/` directly instead of redirecting.** Adopt the documented exact-match pattern\n   (`docs/mcp-auth.md:252-271`) against the named upstream: `location = /mcp/` and\n   `location = /mcp`, both `proxy_pass http://rebar_mcp/mcp;`, each keeping the existing SSE\n   settings. An exact-match location with a URI on `proxy_pass` replaces the matched URI, so\n   `/mcp/` arrives at the app as `/mcp`, `redirect_slashes` never fires, and no Location header\n   is produced. The PREFIX `location /mcp` is retained for `/mcp/...` sub-paths.\n2. **Make a plaintext Location structurally impossible.** Add `proxy_redirect http://$host/\n   https://$host/;` plus the named-upstream form to the MCP locations, so nginx upgrades any\n   `http://` Location an upstream might emit. Scoped to the MCP locations deliberately, because\n   `proxy_redirect` defaults to `default` (derived from that location's own `proxy_pass`), so\n   server-level rules would replace it for `/review/` and `/opcert/` and could break their\n   relative redirects.\n3. **Fix the scheme derivation.** Set `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` on the `mcp` compose service so\n   uvicorn's `ProxyHeadersMiddleware` trusts nginx's forwarded proto. No code change is needed\n   (uvicorn reads the variable natively) and it corrects every app-generated absolute URL. Not a\n   new spoofing risk: nginx sets `X-Forwarded-Proto https` as a LITERAL, overwriting any client\n   value, and the port is published on host loopback with nginx the sole reachable client.\n4. **Add HSTS.** `add_header Strict-Transport-Security \"max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains\"\n   always;` on the 443 server. `always` is required so it is emitted on error responses — the\n   401 the MCP endpoint returns to an unauthenticated client.\n\nNOT changed: `EXPECTED_URL` in `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_client_configs.py` and the\ndocumented/example URLs — after step 1 the trailing-slash form is served directly over https, so\nit stays canonical and `auth_resource_server_url` stays consistent with it. Also NOT changed:\nproduction nginx on the live box; this lands the config in the repo and an operator applies it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The edge routes `/mcp/` straight to the app's `/mcp`, so no Location header is produced\n      for the documented URL. Verified by a structural parse of\n      `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` asserting an exact-match `location = /mcp/` whose\n      `proxy_pass` carries the app path `/mcp`.\n- [ ] An HSTS header with `max-age` of at least 31536000 is served on the 443 server, marked\n      `always` so it is present on the unauthenticated 401. Verified by a structural parse\n      asserting `add_header Strict-Transport-Security \"...\" always;` in that server block.\n- [ ] Each MCP location carries a `proxy_redirect` mapping an `http://` upstream Location to\n      `https://`. Verified by a structural parse that fails when it is absent from any of them.\n- [ ] With the committed `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` value in force, a `/mcp/` request through the\n      real `streamable_http_app()` yields a Location whose scheme is `https`. Verified by an\n      in-process ASGI test through uvicorn's `ProxyHeadersMiddleware`, with an untrusted-peer\n      negative control asserting `http`; plus a structural assertion that\n      `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` is set on the compose `mcp` service.\n- [ ] LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE. `curl -D - https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/`\n      emits NO `http://` Location, and an HSTS header is present. Evidence must be OBSERVED\n      against the deployed edge and recorded in a ticket comment showing the actual response\n      headers. A passing local test is NOT sufficient, and neither is a merged change: it must\n      be deployed and serving. The fix is an edge config change the authoring agent must not\n      apply to the live box, so this depends on an OPERATOR deploying it and must not be ticked\n      on the strength of a local render.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED-first; both tiers observed failing before any fix.\n\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` — structural tests over the committed nginx template\n  (exact-match `/mcp/` and `/mcp` locations, `proxy_redirect` on each MCP location, HSTS with\n  `always`) and over `docker-compose.yml` (`FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` on `mcp`). No nginx binary is\n  available here, so these parse the committed text — as the existing\n  `test_nginx_mcp_location_proxies_to_the_named_upstream` (`:154`) already does.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py` — a behavioural test over the real\n  `streamable_http_app()` through `uvicorn.middleware.proxy_headers.ProxyHeadersMiddleware`\n  configured from the committed compose value, asserting the Location scheme is `https`, with an\n  untrusted-peer negative control asserting `http`. Executable oracle for mechanism B.\n\nMutation check: re-introduce each confirmed cause (drop the exact-match locations, the\n`proxy_redirect`, the HSTS header, `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS`) and confirm the corresponding test\nreturns to RED, then restore. Run inside an OS sandbox.\n\n## File impact\n\n`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`, `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`,\n`tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py`.\n\n## Compat / rollback\n\nAdditive: two exact-match locations ahead of the retained prefix location, two directives per\nMCP location, one HSTS header, one compose env var. `/mcp` returns a 401 today and continues to;\n`/mcp/` stops redirecting and starts serving. No caller depends on the 307 — it is the defect.\nRollback is a revert of the four files. Trust boundary unchanged: the `static` bearer still\ngates `/mcp`, `/health` stays unauthenticated, and `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` only selects which peer\nuvicorn trusts `X-Forwarded-*` from.\n\n## Portability\n\nCommitted config plus tests that parse committed text. No CI provider is involved: the\nstructural tests run under plain `pytest` and the behavioural test is in-process ASGI with no\ndocker and no network. Applying the nginx change is an operator step, not a CI trigger.\n\nCaused by fd4a-4e91-f179-4932."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787860796290868001,"uuid":"9a0273f7-7dc0-40b5-8011-108e2a984c72"}